00:00:41.134 --> 00:00:44.557
<i>Let me tell you a story about a young man called Oliver.</i>


00:00:44.589 --> 00:00:48.974
<i>There's no singing. No dancing.
And definitely no happy ending.</i>


00:00:49.805 --> 00:00:51.662
<i>But before we get to me,</i>


00:00:51.695 --> 00:00:53.999
<i>this all started with a thief
called Tom Chitling.</i>


00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:03.854
There he is!


00:01:03.887 --> 00:01:05.423
Stop! Stop!


00:01:23.631 --> 00:01:25.296
Let's go!


00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.519
- Come here! Where is it?
- I don't have it.


00:02:41.391 --> 00:02:43.983
<i>Growing up,
it was just me and Mum.</i>


00:02:44.014 --> 00:02:47.438
<i>We didn't have a lot,
but we had our imagination.</i>


00:02:48.238 --> 00:02:50.255
Where'd you take us
today, Oliver?


00:02:50.286 --> 00:02:53.166
The beach.
And we had an ice cream.


00:02:53.197 --> 00:02:54.959
Mmm, delicious.


00:02:55.918 --> 00:02:58.861
I took us
to the circus.


00:02:58.894 --> 00:03:01.551
Wow. Elephants.


00:03:01.582 --> 00:03:03.375
- Thanks, Mum.
- You're welcome.


00:03:03.405 --> 00:03:05.743
I'm gonna take us somewhere
even better tomorrow.


00:03:08.526 --> 00:03:10.127
I can't wait.


00:03:13.774 --> 00:03:15.407
What do you see?


00:03:15.437 --> 00:03:17.070
A lady swimming.


00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:18.958
What else?


00:03:19.855 --> 00:03:21.935
What does Oliver see?


00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.822
I don't understand,
Mum.


00:03:23.853 --> 00:03:28.398
Well, I see escape.


00:03:29.647 --> 00:03:32.303
I see a powerful woman


00:03:32.335 --> 00:03:34.383
leaving behind a life
that wasn't meant for her.


00:03:35.919 --> 00:03:39.151
And all of the flowers,
they're telling us why.


00:03:41.198 --> 00:03:44.814
Anyone ever told you
you're a bit weird, Mum?


00:03:45.486 --> 00:03:49.551
Has anyone ever told you
you're a bit cheeky?


00:03:49.581 --> 00:03:51.247
Shh!


00:03:51.279 --> 00:03:55.375
Oh. We're going
to space now, are we?


00:03:55.405 --> 00:03:56.462
Yeah.


00:03:57.678 --> 00:04:00.879
I thought we were supposed to be
doing our dreams for the future.


00:04:02.447 --> 00:04:04.111
I don't get it.


00:04:04.141 --> 00:04:06.958
Well that's you.
And that's me.


00:04:06.991 --> 00:04:08.911
And we're
in a gallery.


00:04:08.941 --> 00:04:12.622
And we're looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery


00:04:12.655 --> 00:04:14.702
looking at this painting
of you and me in a gallery.


00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:16.719
And it goes on
and on and on...


00:04:17.519 --> 00:04:19.534
<i>But nothing
lasts forever.</i>


00:04:26.061 --> 00:04:27.789
<i>Then it was just me.</i>


00:04:27.822 --> 00:04:29.518
Poor lad.


00:04:31.566 --> 00:04:33.038
Time to go, Oliver.


00:04:33.069 --> 00:04:34.734
<i>I didn't know
anyone else.</i>


00:04:36.557 --> 00:04:38.414
<i>I certainly didn't belong
with them.</i>


00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:44.623
<i>I was better off on my own.</i>


00:04:54.606 --> 00:04:56.559
Oi! Wake up.


00:04:57.902 --> 00:04:59.726
Wake up,
you little rat.


00:04:59.758 --> 00:05:01.902
Right. I've told you before,
and I'm not... Hey!


00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.343
I'm not gonna
tell you again!


00:05:03.917 --> 00:05:05.423
Don't you dare.


00:05:05.455 --> 00:05:07.214
Sod off,
you little scrounger!


00:05:07.246 --> 00:05:09.647
Stop sleeping
in the gallery!


00:05:09.678 --> 00:05:12.302
<i>People don't really call
me Oliver any more. They call me...</i>


00:07:06.702 --> 00:07:09.870
Congratulations, love.


00:07:09.902 --> 00:07:11.310
You've won
a little yellow square.


00:07:11.341 --> 00:07:13.005
You could see
I had my hands full.


00:07:13.038 --> 00:07:14.414
They're not my rules.
I just enforce 'em.


00:07:14.446 --> 00:07:15.822
I was right here.


00:07:15.854 --> 00:07:17.166
You was right here
for too long.


00:07:17.198 --> 00:07:18.863
I thought
you were gonna move in.


00:07:18.894 --> 00:07:20.718
Do you think
I like doing this?


00:07:20.749 --> 00:07:23.086
Actually, I do.
It makes me feel big in every way.


00:07:23.118 --> 00:07:24.911
Could you not give
the ticket to anyone else?


00:07:24.942 --> 00:07:26.670
I'm not just giving 'em
to nice people.


00:07:26.701 --> 00:07:28.302
You look like a nice person,
so I've given one to you.


00:07:28.333 --> 00:07:30.158
Please, I was literally
about to leave.


00:07:30.189 --> 00:07:31.534
You should have left earlier,
shouldn't you?


00:07:31.565 --> 00:07:33.230
I can't afford this ticket.


00:07:33.262 --> 00:07:35.279
Well, I can't afford a 4K TV,
but I wish I could.


00:07:35.309 --> 00:07:36.878
I'd like one of those.


00:07:36.909 --> 00:07:38.766
Actually, I don't even know
what it is,


00:07:38.798 --> 00:07:40.878
but I like the sound of owning it.
I wish I could have it.


00:07:40.909 --> 00:07:42.733
- Please, sir...
- Please, please, please.


00:07:42.765 --> 00:07:44.494
Don't tell me
your problems.


00:07:44.525 --> 00:07:46.413
You're gonna get another one
in a minute. Oi!


00:07:46.445 --> 00:07:49.198
Hey, stay away from that van.
That's my van, you little pig.


00:07:59.854 --> 00:08:01.679
- Here you go, miss.
- Thank you.


00:08:09.709 --> 00:08:11.086
Stop that lad!


00:08:28.909 --> 00:08:31.054
Yo, man. The bikes!


00:08:44.397 --> 00:08:45.997
Yo, likkle man!


00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:48.782
Yo!


00:08:49.485 --> 00:08:51.375
- Hey, slow up, bro.
- What?


00:08:52.271 --> 00:08:55.694
Relax, man.
The cops packed it in way back.


00:08:55.725 --> 00:08:57.071
Why are you chasing me then?


00:08:57.102 --> 00:08:58.830
'Cause you forgot
your shopping.


00:09:01.613 --> 00:09:02.830
Okay.


00:09:08.173 --> 00:09:09.262
- It's you, isn't it?
- What?


00:09:09.293 --> 00:09:10.894
Doing all this.


00:09:11.502 --> 00:09:13.390
Come on, man,
we know that it's you.


00:09:13.421 --> 00:09:16.622
We done the forensics
on your spray cans.


00:09:16.653 --> 00:09:18.893
He's a joker, this one.
But, look, listen.


00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:20.845
I am Dodge,
this is Batesy,


00:09:20.877 --> 00:09:22.733
and together we...


00:09:29.678 --> 00:09:31.694
- What about your bikes?
- Not ours, pal!


00:09:39.277 --> 00:09:40.782
Come on!


00:09:43.917 --> 00:09:45.839
Hey! Stop!


00:09:50.893 --> 00:09:52.430
I said get down!


00:10:03.405 --> 00:10:05.902
Come on.


00:10:05.933 --> 00:10:08.141
- Cracking set of pins, love.
- Look at that.


00:10:08.173 --> 00:10:09.678
What happened to him?


00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:12.015
- What was that?
- Brilliant.


00:10:12.045 --> 00:10:13.678
You two again.


00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:16.302
Oh, come on.
We're your guardian angels.


00:10:16.334 --> 00:10:18.062
Where's the other guy?


00:10:18.094 --> 00:10:20.303
Come with us. We'll sort you out
with some new gear.


00:10:20.334 --> 00:10:23.054
Or you could just stay here.
I mean, it's up to you.


00:10:24.237 --> 00:10:25.806
We got trainers as well.


00:10:27.182 --> 00:10:28.718
Really?


00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.797
Come on, handsome.
Follow us.


00:10:35.342 --> 00:10:37.935
- I ain't got anything worth stealing.
- Come on, mate.


00:10:37.966 --> 00:10:40.590
You can't go through
life trusting no one.


00:10:40.622 --> 00:10:42.446
Yeah, we saved
your arse once already.


00:10:42.477 --> 00:10:44.142
That was
the other guy.


00:10:44.173 --> 00:10:46.093
What, you mean Red?


00:10:46.125 --> 00:10:47.983
Yeah.
The guy in the green jacket.


00:10:49.485 --> 00:10:51.630
That's a real hero,
that one.


00:11:00.814 --> 00:11:02.286
<i>Entre, s'il vous plaît.</i>


00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.957
<i>Who's that?</i>


00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:13.262
Just me and Batesy.


00:11:13.294 --> 00:11:14.863
What size waist are you?


00:11:14.894 --> 00:11:17.039
<i>I'd say he's about
a 30 regular.</i>


00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.766
Who's that?


00:11:18.796 --> 00:11:22.830
Oh, that is the ghost
of Dodge's grandpa.


00:11:22.862 --> 00:11:26.191
Batesy, shut up.
I'll introduce you later.


00:11:31.117 --> 00:11:32.941
Let's get you
some clobber first.


00:11:32.974 --> 00:11:34.606
Uh, you do realize
I've got no money?


00:11:34.638 --> 00:11:36.526
It's all right. You can owe us.


00:11:36.557 --> 00:11:38.318
I don't like
owing people.


00:11:40.909 --> 00:11:44.590
Go on, have 'em.
Introductory special offer.


00:11:45.005 --> 00:11:47.629
- We can spare 'em.
- Where did you get all this?


00:11:47.661 --> 00:11:50.542
- Sports Warehouse.
- Oh, I lost my favorite hat on that job.


00:11:50.573 --> 00:11:54.189
Are you ever gonna stop banging
on about that hat?


00:11:54.221 --> 00:11:56.142
- Huh?
- Probably not.


00:11:56.174 --> 00:12:00.205
Have 'em. They cost us nothing,
shop's claimed insurance.


00:12:00.238 --> 00:12:02.735
Plus, them pasty legs...


00:12:03.789 --> 00:12:05.741
they're gonna give me
nightmares.


00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:10.574
Oh, better give 'em a little bit
of a shake actually.


00:12:10.606 --> 00:12:12.879
Better give 'em
a shake first, eh.


00:12:17.773 --> 00:12:20.046
Hey, Fagin.


00:12:22.189 --> 00:12:25.070
Dodge, I've told you before.


00:12:25.102 --> 00:12:27.950
You cannot bring in green kids
off the street.


00:12:27.981 --> 00:12:30.125
- I know, but Fa...
- No buts.


00:12:30.157 --> 00:12:31.629
Out he goes.


00:12:31.661 --> 00:12:34.574
Fagin, please.
This is Twist.


00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:36.846
Extreme graffiti artist.


00:12:36.878 --> 00:12:38.510
Reaching places
others can't reach.


00:12:38.541 --> 00:12:40.462
Tags under moving cranes
and that.


00:12:40.494 --> 00:12:43.278
Like what's his face, uh...
Banksy. Yeah.


00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:46.031
Reaching places other people
can't reach, eh?


00:12:46.861 --> 00:12:50.222
The problem with graffiti is,
is you can't move it.


00:12:50.253 --> 00:12:52.943
What's the point in a painting
if it's always in the same place?


00:12:52.974 --> 00:12:55.854
The higher up I put my work,
the more people can see it.


00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:59.822
That's the point.
It doesn't belong to anybody.


00:12:59.853 --> 00:13:02.191
An idealist, eh?


00:13:02.221 --> 00:13:04.301
All property is theft.


00:13:04.941 --> 00:13:08.270
In my case,
that's literally true.


00:13:09.325 --> 00:13:11.917
Tell me, Mr. Idealist,


00:13:12.461 --> 00:13:14.766
how's virtue treating you?


00:13:14.798 --> 00:13:16.877
Is it filling your stomach?


00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:19.118
Can it give you
a hug on a cold night?


00:13:19.149 --> 00:13:22.478
Ideals are useless.
They're like appendix.


00:13:23.565 --> 00:13:24.813
Cut 'em out.


00:13:24.845 --> 00:13:25.965
He's fast.


00:13:25.998 --> 00:13:28.334
He left the Old Bill for dust.


00:13:28.365 --> 00:13:30.701
I thought maybe
we could train him up


00:13:30.734 --> 00:13:33.038
seeing as
we have a vacancy.


00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:34.477
I'm not a thief.


00:13:34.509 --> 00:13:37.422
What, you've never stole
a sarnie from Tescos?


00:13:37.453 --> 00:13:40.717
I don't need to. They chuck out
enough if you know where to look.


00:13:40.749 --> 00:13:42.829
Oh, living the dream.


00:13:42.861 --> 00:13:45.165
We all have to start somewhere,
don't we?


00:13:45.197 --> 00:13:48.046
It wasn't so long ago that you
were stealing credit card details.


00:13:48.078 --> 00:13:49.517
Uh, it's called phishing.


00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:51.693
It's called surviving.


00:13:51.726 --> 00:13:54.606
It's what we do
to survive.


00:13:55.533 --> 00:13:57.998
- Suppose.
- Bravo.


00:13:58.029 --> 00:13:59.374
You need a place to stay?


00:14:02.062 --> 00:14:03.214
No. Thank you.


00:14:04.046 --> 00:14:06.734
Cheers for the clothes.
I'll pay you back.


00:14:11.437 --> 00:14:13.677
That's
a really decent copy.


00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:16.526
I've seen the original tons
of times at the Tate.


00:14:16.556 --> 00:14:17.678
No, you haven't.


00:14:24.398 --> 00:14:26.862
I tell you what.
I'll cook tonight, Dodge.


00:14:26.893 --> 00:14:29.005
What do you want,
spaghetti or beef burgers?


00:14:29.036 --> 00:14:30.637
- I love the...
- Ah, nah.


00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:32.109
Come on. Do me a flavor, Fag.


00:14:32.141 --> 00:14:34.893
You know I'm 72% vegan.
Meat is a treat.


00:14:34.925 --> 00:14:38.285
Doesn't matter what you eat
so long as you eat together.


00:14:38.318 --> 00:14:41.486
Because, as I've always said,
the most important thing


00:14:41.517 --> 00:14:44.045
is the family
that eats together...


00:14:44.077 --> 00:14:45.997
...stays together.


00:14:46.029 --> 00:14:47.790
Yeah. Right.


00:14:56.621 --> 00:14:58.637
Oi! Mate.


00:14:59.596 --> 00:15:01.230
I just wanted to...


00:15:02.606 --> 00:15:04.110
Stand there gawping
like a fish?


00:15:04.845 --> 00:15:07.053
If you could speak sometime
soon that'd be great


00:15:07.084 --> 00:15:08.557
- 'cause I've got somewhere to go.
- I'm sorry.


00:15:08.588 --> 00:15:10.413
I didn't realize you,
you were a...


00:15:10.446 --> 00:15:12.013
And I didn't recognize you
with clothes on.


00:15:12.046 --> 00:15:13.485
I just wanted to say thanks.


00:15:13.517 --> 00:15:15.086
You're welcome.


00:15:16.205 --> 00:15:17.645
Is that everything?


00:15:19.246 --> 00:15:20.814
I'll take that as a yes.


00:16:48.076 --> 00:16:49.997
The boy's an artist.


00:16:50.029 --> 00:16:51.918
So, what do you see?


00:16:51.949 --> 00:16:54.605
A loner with a cracking pair
of trainers?


00:16:55.534 --> 00:16:57.966
Well, that's disappointing.
You missed the point.


00:17:00.621 --> 00:17:02.542
Can you get up there?


00:17:02.573 --> 00:17:04.557
Please. If he can...


00:17:05.198 --> 00:17:07.662
- Yeah.
- Some boys like respect.


00:17:08.493 --> 00:17:11.917
Some boys like being
in the pecking order.


00:17:11.949 --> 00:17:13.166
But this one...


00:17:13.774 --> 00:17:16.236
he wants something
that he's missing.


00:17:16.268 --> 00:17:17.710
A smartphone?


00:17:20.076 --> 00:17:21.517
He wants love.


00:17:21.549 --> 00:17:23.694
So let's give it
to him.


00:17:58.253 --> 00:18:00.334
Glad I climbed up
this side.


00:18:00.365 --> 00:18:01.453
Sorry!


00:18:01.486 --> 00:18:03.599
There's no toilet
up here.


00:18:04.078 --> 00:18:05.838
Love what you've done
with the place.


00:18:05.869 --> 00:18:08.078
It's just while
I'm doing this one here.


00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:12.333
Gonna offer me
a cup of tea then, or...


00:18:12.365 --> 00:18:14.766
I could do you cream crackers
and chocolate spread.


00:18:14.796 --> 00:18:16.430
Ooh, nutritious.


00:18:18.316 --> 00:18:20.237
I thought you were
a guy, by the way.


00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:22.094
That's why I was being
weird earlier.


00:18:22.124 --> 00:18:23.341
You say
the sweetest things.


00:18:23.372 --> 00:18:25.805
No, no. I wasn't...


00:18:25.838 --> 00:18:28.270
I mean, I just...


00:18:28.302 --> 00:18:31.725
- The way you move...
- Like a guy? Yeah. I get it.


00:18:32.462 --> 00:18:35.502
- I don't mean to offend you.
- Oh, why would that offend me?


00:18:35.533 --> 00:18:36.653
Just guys are more strong.


00:18:37.324 --> 00:18:39.149
Not that girls aren't strong.


00:18:39.182 --> 00:18:40.654
Girls are strong as well.


00:18:40.686 --> 00:18:42.574
Just guys tend to be...
I don't know.


00:18:42.606 --> 00:18:44.589
Not much of
a smooth talker, are we?


00:18:45.197 --> 00:18:46.958
Best stick to climbing
I think.


00:18:48.782 --> 00:18:50.414
How come you're so good
at climbing anyway?


00:18:53.996 --> 00:18:56.845
When I was younger,
I felt safer up high.


00:18:57.996 --> 00:18:59.598
People couldn't find me.


00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:03.501
So I taught myself
to climb.


00:19:03.981 --> 00:19:06.126
And you've been a loner
on a roof ever since?


00:19:06.796 --> 00:19:08.557
Suits me just fine.


00:19:09.901 --> 00:19:11.405
Well, you can't stay
up here forever.


00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:14.349
Isn't there things you wanna
see, things you wanna experience?


00:19:14.382 --> 00:19:16.014
Must get pretty boring.


00:19:16.045 --> 00:19:17.646
I can go anywhere I want.


00:19:19.149 --> 00:19:20.494
- What?
- See.


00:19:33.421 --> 00:19:34.862
I can imagine.


00:19:34.893 --> 00:19:37.901
Well, I'm here
in real life,


00:19:38.316 --> 00:19:41.005
and I've come to invite you
to a real-life dinner.


00:19:41.036 --> 00:19:42.605
Me and you?


00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.957
Come to Fagin's,
tonight at 7:00.


00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:49.453
And you never know,


00:19:49.485 --> 00:19:52.079
we might just be better
company than your paintings.


00:20:28.014 --> 00:20:29.294
What am I doing?


00:20:29.326 --> 00:20:30.989
What does Oliver see?


00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:33.902
Mum?


00:20:38.284 --> 00:20:39.693
Can't be by yourself forever.


00:20:44.941 --> 00:20:47.084
You're late.


00:20:47.116 --> 00:20:49.357
Is that any way to greet
your favorite supplier?


00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:54.733
What happened to Tom?


00:20:55.276 --> 00:20:57.133
He screwed up.
That's what happened.


00:20:57.966 --> 00:21:00.814
My kids are not disposable.


00:21:00.846 --> 00:21:03.406
That's exactly what they are,
my old friend.


00:21:04.141 --> 00:21:06.957
No friends, no family.
No questions.


00:21:14.764 --> 00:21:16.717
For complications.


00:21:23.052 --> 00:21:25.292
Did you get my envelope?


00:21:25.325 --> 00:21:26.830
What, this?


00:21:28.621 --> 00:21:30.254
When has it ever been
that easy, eh?


00:21:31.628 --> 00:21:33.068
I want in.


00:21:33.101 --> 00:21:34.989
I know you're pulling
a job.


00:21:35.021 --> 00:21:36.813
You're hitting Losberne.


00:21:37.292 --> 00:21:38.924
I want a cut.


00:21:38.957 --> 00:21:40.140
I was gonna tell you.


00:21:40.173 --> 00:21:41.326
Of course you were.


00:21:41.356 --> 00:21:43.085
Let me make it
easy for you.


00:21:43.117 --> 00:21:44.462
Whatever's in there...


00:21:45.549 --> 00:21:47.405
seems very important
to your little plan.


00:21:47.437 --> 00:21:49.677
Question is, are we gonna do it
the easy or the hard way?


00:21:59.405 --> 00:22:00.973
Partners.


00:22:07.885 --> 00:22:10.413
Partners. Now...


00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:13.229
the envelope.


00:22:14.252 --> 00:22:15.437
I think I'll keep it.


00:22:16.525 --> 00:22:18.958
Just in case
of future complications.


00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:38.574
Yeah.


00:22:38.604 --> 00:22:42.221
Took your bloody...
Oh, my giddy aunt.


00:22:42.253 --> 00:22:44.589
What is happening
with your barnet?


00:22:44.621 --> 00:22:47.085
Sorry.
Sorry, sorry, sorry.


00:22:47.116 --> 00:22:49.806
Come on, look, look.
Welcome, Twist.


00:22:49.837 --> 00:22:54.158
Let me take your jean shirt,
jacket for you. There we go.


00:22:55.820 --> 00:22:57.517
- Come on.
- Ah.


00:22:57.548 --> 00:22:59.372
Glad you could make it,
mate.


00:22:59.405 --> 00:23:01.869
Oh, Twist.
Come and sit next to me.


00:23:05.454 --> 00:23:08.557
Oh, blimey, look. Nancy,
take his beautiful flowers


00:23:08.589 --> 00:23:09.870
and put them in some water.


00:23:11.213 --> 00:23:12.333
Mmm.


00:23:14.989 --> 00:23:16.652
He can call me that.


00:23:16.685 --> 00:23:17.965
- You don't.
- Understood.


00:23:17.997 --> 00:23:21.421
I am starving.


00:23:21.453 --> 00:23:22.861
Dodge, please.


00:23:22.893 --> 00:23:24.622
Fagin, can we just
talk about something?


00:23:24.654 --> 00:23:26.830
Can we talk about our boy,
Batesy here,


00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:28.685
stealing my food
from under my bed?


00:23:28.716 --> 00:23:30.636
- Grass.
- Thief.


00:23:30.668 --> 00:23:33.294
- Okay, we're all thieves.
- Yeah, be a better one is the point.


00:23:33.324 --> 00:23:35.436
All right. Okay, okay.


00:23:35.469 --> 00:23:37.710
Uh, Twist,


00:23:37.741 --> 00:23:41.164
I want you to say a few words
because it's a tradition.


00:23:41.197 --> 00:23:43.726
About how thankful you are.


00:23:45.036 --> 00:23:48.717
Well, thanks for having me
round for dinner, I suppose.


00:23:48.749 --> 00:23:51.469
I can't remember the last time
that I sat down...


00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:53.166
Like a family?


00:23:54.189 --> 00:23:56.206
We're all orphans here.


00:24:01.901 --> 00:24:03.310
All right,
that's the thanks.


00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:04.973
Cool, um,
can we bloody eat now?


00:24:05.005 --> 00:24:07.054
- Yes! Eat. Eat.
- All right!


00:24:07.084 --> 00:24:09.004
- Eat.
- All right, all right.


00:24:09.037 --> 00:24:10.798
Let's go.


00:24:10.828 --> 00:24:12.302
Mmm.


00:24:20.525 --> 00:24:22.926
It appears that
you're a connoisseur of beauty.


00:24:23.597 --> 00:24:28.238
Yeah. I saw you in my office
admiring my collection, Mr. Twist.


00:24:29.325 --> 00:24:31.245
Can I stop using that name?


00:24:31.277 --> 00:24:33.613
It makes me sound
as though I'm in a casino.


00:24:34.604 --> 00:24:35.884
What else can I call you?


00:24:36.685 --> 00:24:37.708
Oliver.


00:24:37.740 --> 00:24:40.364
Oliver. Well, Oliver,


00:24:40.396 --> 00:24:42.700
your artwork is impressive.


00:24:42.733 --> 00:24:44.398
They're just copies.


00:24:44.429 --> 00:24:47.085
No, nothing is just a copy.
We always put a little bit


00:24:47.116 --> 00:24:49.133
of soul into everything,
don't you think?


00:24:50.349 --> 00:24:52.813
- Yeah, I suppose.
- When I was your age,


00:24:52.844 --> 00:24:54.893
I wanted to be an artist,
just like you.


00:24:55.373 --> 00:24:57.645
But my father was tasteless.
A bully.


00:24:57.676 --> 00:24:59.406
Oh, I'm sorry.


00:24:59.436 --> 00:25:02.285
Why sorry?
This is all my art, and Nancy...


00:25:03.468 --> 00:25:05.101
is my masterpiece.


00:25:05.517 --> 00:25:07.597
She needs someone to train with.


00:25:07.629 --> 00:25:09.901
Someone who can keep up
with her.


00:25:10.668 --> 00:25:14.828
- So you all just do whatever you want?
- Yes. But together.


00:25:14.861 --> 00:25:16.300
We never work alone.


00:25:16.332 --> 00:25:19.884
You know, we live together,
we eat together.


00:25:19.916 --> 00:25:21.644
Because the family
that eats together...


00:25:21.677 --> 00:25:23.532
Stays together. I know.


00:25:25.708 --> 00:25:26.797
Watch this,
watch this.


00:25:27.789 --> 00:25:29.614
Got a little surprise
for you.


00:25:29.644 --> 00:25:31.149
- For me?
- Yeah.


00:25:41.197 --> 00:25:42.509
Come on, then.


00:25:43.117 --> 00:25:45.453
You ready?
We're going out.


00:25:45.996 --> 00:25:47.598
Come on.


00:25:47.628 --> 00:25:50.477
Make sure you bring him back
in one piece.


00:26:00.877 --> 00:26:02.669
Don't you guys
ever feel bad?


00:26:03.245 --> 00:26:05.677
What? No.


00:26:05.709 --> 00:26:08.077
Look, the people that
we target are criminals anyway.


00:26:08.108 --> 00:26:10.798
So, it's justified,
innit?


00:26:10.828 --> 00:26:13.708
Think of Fagin
as good old Robin Hood


00:26:13.741 --> 00:26:15.373
and we're his Merry Men.


00:26:15.404 --> 00:26:16.653
Hmm.


00:26:43.341 --> 00:26:44.878
Oliver.


00:26:45.997 --> 00:26:47.244
Oliver.


00:26:47.277 --> 00:26:49.678
Hey, wake up. Come on.


00:26:51.085 --> 00:26:53.006
Get changed.
We're going out.


00:26:55.053 --> 00:26:56.493
Okay, give me a sec.


00:27:02.317 --> 00:27:04.814
- So, are you sticking around?
- Yeah, I think I will.


00:27:04.845 --> 00:27:06.669
You sure
you wanna do this?


00:27:06.701 --> 00:27:09.485
Yeah. It's nice
to belong to something.


00:27:10.349 --> 00:27:11.917
Trust me, you'll be fine.


00:27:25.421 --> 00:27:26.829
Morning, Dr. Losberne.


00:27:29.100 --> 00:27:30.285
Good morning.


00:27:34.189 --> 00:27:37.293
Dr. Crispin Losberne.


00:27:39.244 --> 00:27:41.261
Curator, art dealer


00:27:41.292 --> 00:27:44.844
and connoisseur
of 18th-century painters.


00:27:44.877 --> 00:27:47.405
He's very predictable,
which helps.


00:27:47.436 --> 00:27:52.653
Gets up every morning and leaves
for work at eight o'clock sharp.


00:27:52.685 --> 00:27:55.309
<i>He looks at his messages</i>


00:27:55.341 --> 00:27:59.245
<i>and he puts his phone away in the
right-hand pocket of his coat.</i>


00:27:59.276 --> 00:28:02.188
- Flat white.
- <i>Pays the barista.</i>


00:28:02.221 --> 00:28:04.045
Then he drinks his coffee.


00:28:04.077 --> 00:28:05.837
- Hmm.
- What's all this about?


00:28:05.868 --> 00:28:08.140
Well, we're gonna borrow
his phone.


00:28:08.172 --> 00:28:11.085
And have it back in his pocket
before he knows it's gone.


00:28:11.116 --> 00:28:12.556
But why?


00:28:12.589 --> 00:28:14.381
He took everything from me.


00:28:14.413 --> 00:28:15.597
Everything.


00:28:17.292 --> 00:28:20.076
And I'm going
to return the favor.


00:28:20.587 --> 00:28:23.853
First thing, we need
to hack Losberne's phone.


00:28:24.429 --> 00:28:26.733
Oh, and as far as the day
is concerned,


00:28:26.764 --> 00:28:28.204
it's all performance art.


00:28:28.237 --> 00:28:31.630
And the performance
will be given by Nancy.


00:28:34.028 --> 00:28:35.310
Oh!


00:28:35.340 --> 00:28:36.652
I am such a klutz.


00:28:36.685 --> 00:28:38.604
Let me help.
I've got tissues in my bag.


00:28:38.637 --> 00:28:40.110
You absolutely must
let me help.


00:28:40.141 --> 00:28:42.509
God, it's all over
your lovely jacket.


00:28:42.541 --> 00:28:43.950
Oh, I'm so stupid.


00:28:48.876 --> 00:28:50.380
I was on my way
to the Royal Academy


00:28:50.413 --> 00:28:51.885
to see
the Gainsborough exhibition.


00:28:51.916 --> 00:28:53.613
- Really.
- Oh, have you been?


00:28:56.205 --> 00:28:58.125
As a matter of fact,
I curated it.


00:28:58.156 --> 00:29:00.973
- Really?
- Oh, yes. Come on.


00:29:01.004 --> 00:29:03.214
- <i>Dodge, you got it yet?</i>
- Yeah, plugging in.


00:29:04.268 --> 00:29:07.564
All right.
On its way, Batesy.


00:29:07.596 --> 00:29:09.869
I'm quite a mover and shaker
in the art world.


00:29:09.900 --> 00:29:10.925
I have my own place.


00:29:10.957 --> 00:29:12.206
You have
your own gallery?


00:29:13.165 --> 00:29:14.828
<i>That working, Bates?</i>


00:29:14.860 --> 00:29:16.942
You don't ever need interns,
do you?


00:29:16.973 --> 00:29:18.092
Never say never.


00:29:19.821 --> 00:29:21.133
<i>Come on, Batesy.
Hurry up.</i>


00:29:21.164 --> 00:29:22.797
I'll give you my card.


00:29:22.829 --> 00:29:24.877
<i>I'm going as quick as I can.</i>


00:29:24.907 --> 00:29:26.189
It's in my jacket.


00:29:26.221 --> 00:29:27.373
Oh.


00:29:29.133 --> 00:29:30.669
<i>We need
to speed this up.</i>


00:29:30.701 --> 00:29:33.101
Yes, of course.


00:29:34.956 --> 00:29:36.365
- Oh.
- Bit wet.


00:29:36.396 --> 00:29:38.092
Hurry up,
hurry up, hurry up.


00:29:38.125 --> 00:29:39.725
Pop by anytime.


00:29:40.717 --> 00:29:43.438
- Goodbye.
- Dodge, quick, he's leaving.


00:29:47.820 --> 00:29:48.942
Quickly!


00:29:49.389 --> 00:29:50.862
Yes. Let's go.


00:29:57.644 --> 00:29:59.533
Garages on Swift Road.


00:30:09.037 --> 00:30:10.766
Someone's taken my phone.


00:30:25.068 --> 00:30:26.220
Get out of my taxi!


00:30:26.252 --> 00:30:28.302
Sorry, mate.
I thought it was free.


00:30:30.316 --> 00:30:32.044
- God.
- Is that what you're looking for?


00:30:33.869 --> 00:30:36.270
Yes. Thank you.


00:30:36.300 --> 00:30:38.668
You can keep the taxi.
I'm going to walk.


00:30:38.701 --> 00:30:40.493
Cheers.


00:30:43.597 --> 00:30:45.101
Where to, guv?


00:30:47.180 --> 00:30:48.845
Not bad for your first job,
Oliver.


00:30:48.876 --> 00:30:51.052
Yeah, and that was just
the hors d'oeuvre.


00:30:51.789 --> 00:30:54.796
Batesy, keep hacking.


00:30:54.829 --> 00:30:57.741
One word from Losberne,
I wanna hear it.


00:30:57.773 --> 00:31:00.334
We need to know his every move.


00:31:01.004 --> 00:31:02.508
- Dodge?
- Yeah?


00:31:02.541 --> 00:31:03.852
Do the washing up.


00:31:03.885 --> 00:31:06.061
Oh, man.


00:31:06.092 --> 00:31:08.364
Nancy, you're going
to art school.


00:31:08.396 --> 00:31:09.869
What?


00:31:09.900 --> 00:31:11.981
It's a crash course.


00:31:12.012 --> 00:31:14.348
If you're gonna be convincing
as an art student


00:31:14.381 --> 00:31:16.205
for an evening,
or even for ten minutes,


00:31:16.236 --> 00:31:18.636
you're gonna have to know
some art to talk about.


00:31:19.532 --> 00:31:21.516
Oliver, would you mind?


00:31:21.548 --> 00:31:23.373
- Of course.
- Ah, good.


00:31:23.822 --> 00:31:25.933
But nothing beats seeing
it in the flesh.


00:31:27.436 --> 00:31:29.357
This is about
Pope Nicholas.


00:31:30.093 --> 00:31:31.629
He's fuming.


00:31:31.661 --> 00:31:33.452
And Dante's... Shit.


00:31:34.125 --> 00:31:35.181
Wha...


00:31:35.564 --> 00:31:37.101
Guard.


00:31:37.900 --> 00:31:39.756
You do realize
this gallery's free, yeah?


00:31:39.788 --> 00:31:42.028
He's worked here
for years. He hates me.


00:31:42.060 --> 00:31:44.012
He's always throwing me out
for sleeping here.


00:31:45.452 --> 00:31:47.821
Get up.
Here, I got you.


00:31:49.357 --> 00:31:50.733
He doesn't scare me.


00:31:53.645 --> 00:31:55.181
Shall we...


00:32:04.876 --> 00:32:06.222
Millais's a genius.


00:32:07.182 --> 00:32:10.701
- The use of...
- Hardly gonna win the 500-meter backstroke, though, is she?


00:32:12.619 --> 00:32:14.350
I'm joking.
I know it's Ophelia.


00:32:15.500 --> 00:32:17.101
Anything else
you'd like to add?


00:32:18.667 --> 00:32:20.460
Well, personally,


00:32:20.491 --> 00:32:21.996
I think the flowers
in the painting


00:32:22.029 --> 00:32:23.917
are as important
as Ophelia herself.


00:32:24.428 --> 00:32:26.764
The floating flowers,
they represent her sorrow.


00:32:26.797 --> 00:32:29.037
And the nettles growing
around the willow,


00:32:29.068 --> 00:32:30.669
well that's...
that's her pain.


00:32:31.820 --> 00:32:33.549
Exactly.


00:32:33.580 --> 00:32:35.309
Did you do art
at school?


00:32:35.340 --> 00:32:38.444
No. It's just
common sense, innit?


00:32:38.476 --> 00:32:41.101
Well, that
and the Internet.


00:32:41.133 --> 00:32:43.341
All right.
Let's see what else you got.


00:32:52.620 --> 00:32:55.981
So, do you feel ready to be the most
convincing art student of all time?


00:32:56.012 --> 00:32:58.413
Yeah. Totally.


00:32:58.444 --> 00:33:00.524
Although no thanks
to my teacher. He was rubbish.


00:33:00.555 --> 00:33:01.868
Oi!


00:33:03.469 --> 00:33:04.622
So, uh...


00:33:05.772 --> 00:33:07.725
couldn't help
but notice old Ophelia


00:33:07.757 --> 00:33:09.485
made quite an impression
on you in there.


00:33:10.315 --> 00:33:11.854
Yeah.


00:33:12.972 --> 00:33:14.348
What was it about her?


00:33:18.028 --> 00:33:19.981
I used to go to
that gallery with my mum.


00:33:21.067 --> 00:33:22.412
She was an artist.


00:33:22.444 --> 00:33:24.876
Right.
That makes sense.


00:33:26.317 --> 00:33:28.589
- So, you did have a family?
- Just a mum.


00:33:29.804 --> 00:33:31.662
She wasn't around
for too long.


00:33:33.229 --> 00:33:34.957
Did you?


00:33:34.989 --> 00:33:36.460
Just a dad.


00:33:36.491 --> 00:33:38.188
But he was around
for too long.


00:33:41.227 --> 00:33:43.021
So why did you get
into free running then?


00:33:44.556 --> 00:33:45.806
So I could escape.


00:33:46.604 --> 00:33:47.949
Escape from what?


00:33:50.220 --> 00:33:52.108
From boys called
Oliver Twist.


00:33:57.676 --> 00:33:59.116
Come here!


00:34:00.300 --> 00:34:04.813
<i>To pull this job off, we'll
need the plans for Losberne's gallery.</i>


00:34:06.060 --> 00:34:07.980
<i>Oh, not
the caterpillar tash.</i>


00:34:08.011 --> 00:34:09.580
- Hello.
- Good morning, sir.


00:34:09.613 --> 00:34:11.341
We spoke on the telephone


00:34:11.373 --> 00:34:14.317
about your conversion
of number 30.


00:34:14.348 --> 00:34:15.788
The Losberne Gallery?


00:34:15.821 --> 00:34:18.477
I have bought
the building opposite


00:34:18.509 --> 00:34:22.444
and I want you to make it modern
like number 30.


00:34:22.476 --> 00:34:25.356
I have the plans here. I can show
you what we did for Dr. Losberne.


00:34:25.387 --> 00:34:27.020
Follow me.


00:34:29.581 --> 00:34:32.428
Yes. Very nice,
very nice.


00:34:35.468 --> 00:34:36.461
<i>Da.</i>


00:34:36.492 --> 00:34:39.404
11:05 on the dot, Fagin.


00:34:39.435 --> 00:34:41.068
Just like you said.


00:34:52.205 --> 00:34:54.093
This is private.


00:34:54.125 --> 00:34:56.621
It's okay.
I don't understand Russian, so...


00:34:58.125 --> 00:34:59.725
You want my business?


00:35:00.652 --> 00:35:03.149
Certainly.
Take your time.


00:35:03.180 --> 00:35:04.588
Thank you.


00:35:14.701 --> 00:35:17.773
No windows, reinforced walls.


00:35:18.764 --> 00:35:19.757
That's the one.


00:35:20.331 --> 00:35:22.444
That'll be
a job getting in.


00:35:22.476 --> 00:35:23.981
We don't have to do that.


00:35:24.524 --> 00:35:27.244
If we do
what I've got planned,


00:35:27.725 --> 00:35:29.293
they bring it out.


00:35:29.324 --> 00:35:30.636
Batesy, carry on.


00:35:30.667 --> 00:35:32.045
Bring what out?


00:35:32.621 --> 00:35:36.204
This is the painting
we're gonna steal.


00:35:36.236 --> 00:35:39.373
One of six paintings
by William Hogarth.


00:35:39.405 --> 00:35:42.093
That says Dotheboy's
Auction House, Fagin.


00:35:42.124 --> 00:35:43.660
Why are we casing up Losberne?


00:35:43.693 --> 00:35:45.485
The painting
was lost in a fire,


00:35:45.517 --> 00:35:48.428
but many people believed
it was a cover-up for a theft.


00:35:48.460 --> 00:35:51.629
All this time,
it's been off the radar.


00:35:51.660 --> 00:35:54.381
So you're saying
Losberne's got it?


00:35:54.413 --> 00:35:56.492
- He's the seller.
- Wait, hang about.


00:35:56.524 --> 00:35:58.060
How did he get his hands on it?


00:35:58.092 --> 00:36:01.133
Many years ago,
Losberne went into partnership


00:36:01.164 --> 00:36:03.212
with a man called
Isaac Solomon.


00:36:03.244 --> 00:36:05.644
Both of them bought
a lot of paintings.


00:36:05.676 --> 00:36:08.044
One of them was the Hogarth.


00:36:08.075 --> 00:36:09.899
But when they had it in auction,


00:36:09.931 --> 00:36:13.644
Losberne went missing
with the paintings.


00:36:13.675 --> 00:36:16.140
- Oh.
- And Solomon had nothing,


00:36:16.172 --> 00:36:19.340
and his credibility
as an art dealer was gone.


00:36:19.820 --> 00:36:23.373
Later, Losberne said
the paintings had been stolen.


00:36:23.405 --> 00:36:24.780
So my man tells me.


00:36:25.644 --> 00:36:28.205
How long have you been there?
I didn't hear you come in.


00:36:28.236 --> 00:36:29.836
You should be more careful,
Fagin.


00:36:29.868 --> 00:36:31.596
You're getting sloppy
in your old age.


00:36:35.500 --> 00:36:36.973
Oh,
it's only you two.


00:36:37.005 --> 00:36:40.429
Oliver, there's someone
I'd like you to meet.


00:36:42.187 --> 00:36:43.180
Oliver.


00:36:45.645 --> 00:36:46.925
Here, boy.


00:36:47.405 --> 00:36:49.164
This is Bullseye.


00:36:49.196 --> 00:36:50.252
Aw...


00:36:50.731 --> 00:36:52.972
You're gonna need
your hands later.


00:36:54.795 --> 00:36:56.428
Round two.


00:36:58.892 --> 00:37:00.429
Magnetic, see?


00:37:00.844 --> 00:37:02.604
Stick it on a pipe and get out.


00:37:13.196 --> 00:37:14.956
Oh, I'm so sorry.
Is it a bad time?


00:37:16.204 --> 00:37:17.612
It's the perfect time.


00:37:27.755 --> 00:37:29.484
Thank you.


00:37:30.443 --> 00:37:31.436
Bottoms up.


00:37:31.469 --> 00:37:32.877
Oh.


00:37:33.612 --> 00:37:35.021
Cheers.


00:37:40.747 --> 00:37:42.667
So, you were saying
it'd be answering the phones,


00:37:42.699 --> 00:37:44.491
doing a little bit of filing?


00:37:44.523 --> 00:37:46.860
Nothing a girl
like you couldn't handle.


00:37:47.437 --> 00:37:50.157
I did actually want
to show you some of my art.


00:37:50.892 --> 00:37:52.333
Street art, you say?


00:37:52.364 --> 00:37:54.157
Yeah,
it's just on here.


00:37:57.997 --> 00:37:59.532
<i>Let me just find them.</i>


00:38:00.204 --> 00:38:01.773
<i>Uh, yes. Okay.</i>


00:38:02.380 --> 00:38:03.725
This one is actually
based on...


00:38:03.756 --> 00:38:05.644
William Blake.
Of course.


00:38:07.756 --> 00:38:09.868
I love what you've done
with the line there.


00:38:11.020 --> 00:38:13.292
<i>These are actually
rather intriguing.</i>


00:38:13.324 --> 00:38:14.380
<i>Don't gas me.</i>


00:38:15.820 --> 00:38:17.356
Come on, girl.


00:38:17.387 --> 00:38:18.573
Give her a second.


00:38:18.604 --> 00:38:20.524
Sorry,
that's my graffiti talk.


00:38:20.556 --> 00:38:22.829
It's the only way to get taken
seriously on the street.


00:38:24.203 --> 00:38:25.837
Oh, right.


00:38:25.867 --> 00:38:27.661
Well, don't forget
your wine.


00:38:27.692 --> 00:38:29.707
Do you know, it's just going
straight through me.


00:38:29.739 --> 00:38:31.660
I must pop to
the little girls' room.


00:38:37.868 --> 00:38:39.341
Is it downstairs, or...


00:38:40.332 --> 00:38:41.612
Straight down
the stairs.


00:38:41.644 --> 00:38:43.116
The door straight
in front of you.


00:38:45.323 --> 00:38:47.212
Okay. Thanks.


00:39:02.668 --> 00:39:05.388
Oh, no. No, no, no.
He's on the move.


00:39:13.836 --> 00:39:16.588
- <i>I could have blown my hand off.</i>
- Yeah, calm down.


00:39:16.621 --> 00:39:18.860
- Everything all right?
- Yes, I'll be up in a minute.


00:39:18.893 --> 00:39:20.717
You better have brought
a spare.


00:39:20.748 --> 00:39:21.741
Uh...


00:39:25.709 --> 00:39:27.437
We just gotta get it
to her.


00:39:27.468 --> 00:39:28.493
I'll take it.


00:39:28.876 --> 00:39:30.317
I'm the climber,
right?


00:39:30.347 --> 00:39:32.620
Whatever you do,
don't drop it.


00:40:05.068 --> 00:40:06.956
Red, it's me.
Let me in.


00:40:10.892 --> 00:40:12.269
Look out.


00:40:13.547 --> 00:40:15.341
- Oh, my God.
- Be careful.


00:40:15.372 --> 00:40:16.748
Okay...


00:40:19.500 --> 00:40:21.164
What's going on
down there?


00:40:31.276 --> 00:40:32.556
Losberne Gallery.


00:40:32.588 --> 00:40:33.773
Special delivery.


00:40:33.804 --> 00:40:35.500
At this time of night?


00:40:35.532 --> 00:40:37.548
I'm right outside, mate.
Got a large package.


00:40:37.579 --> 00:40:40.171
Says, "artworks, fragile."


00:40:40.203 --> 00:40:42.476
I could leave it
on the doorstep if you want?


00:40:42.508 --> 00:40:44.076
No, no, no.
I'm coming. I'm coming.


00:40:44.108 --> 00:40:45.965
I was just in
the middle of something.


00:40:45.996 --> 00:40:47.116
One second.


00:40:47.627 --> 00:40:50.093
I'm at the window.
Where are you?


00:40:50.123 --> 00:40:52.172
<i>Um, let me
just check on that.</i>


00:40:52.204 --> 00:40:53.965
Sorry, mate. Wrong number.


00:41:04.523 --> 00:41:08.171
I wouldn't use that lav...
uh, bathroom for a bit.


00:41:09.004 --> 00:41:11.404
I'm sorry. You're going to have
to wait here for a moment.


00:41:11.436 --> 00:41:12.941
Brittles?


00:41:12.971 --> 00:41:14.412
Can you come up here, please?


00:41:22.733 --> 00:41:24.301
What is this?


00:41:28.268 --> 00:41:30.028
Search her bag.


00:41:30.572 --> 00:41:31.597
Hey!


00:41:32.267 --> 00:41:33.483
Excuse me!


00:41:38.284 --> 00:41:40.044
If that's the way
you treat all your interns,


00:41:40.075 --> 00:41:41.324
you can take
your work experience


00:41:41.355 --> 00:41:42.765
and shove it up your arse!


00:42:04.267 --> 00:42:05.900
Okay.


00:42:29.580 --> 00:42:32.652
<i>Our Dr. Losberne is gonna
get a surprise in the morning.</i>


00:42:32.683 --> 00:42:34.827
Until then,
you can take the night off.


00:42:34.860 --> 00:42:37.228
- Go out, have some fun.
- Yes!


00:42:37.260 --> 00:42:39.275
Yeah, but wait a minute.
Not too much fun


00:42:39.308 --> 00:42:41.676
because you're back
on duty at 7:00 a.m.


00:42:41.708 --> 00:42:42.763
7:00?


00:42:42.795 --> 00:42:44.619
We've all gotta be ready


00:42:44.652 --> 00:42:46.413
to move when
the phone goes.


00:42:46.443 --> 00:42:48.428
And I'll stay tuned to Losberne.


00:42:48.459 --> 00:42:51.628
Well, you know he might be
into some heavy phone sex,


00:42:51.660 --> 00:42:54.220
which means you might be in
for a steamy night, old boy.


00:42:54.251 --> 00:42:56.108
So there's this party.


00:42:56.140 --> 00:42:57.868
- What you saying?
- Red, you coming?


00:42:57.900 --> 00:42:59.340
She got plans.


00:43:03.500 --> 00:43:05.068
You did good.


00:43:17.931 --> 00:43:19.628
Mate, let's go.
Come on.


00:43:20.236 --> 00:43:21.581
Awkward.


00:43:36.140 --> 00:43:39.276
Come on, mate. Don't be such
a Debbie Downer.


00:43:39.307 --> 00:43:41.868
You know, there are
other birds in London.


00:43:42.348 --> 00:43:44.172
Come on.
Have a drink with us.


00:43:44.203 --> 00:43:46.540
No, I'm all right, mate.
Honestly.


00:43:46.571 --> 00:43:48.523
Come on.
You know you want to.


00:43:48.555 --> 00:43:49.804
Seriously, Batesy.


00:43:50.284 --> 00:43:51.661
I'm all right here.


00:43:52.523 --> 00:43:54.059
All right. Fine.


00:44:02.764 --> 00:44:04.333
- Hey.
- I said...


00:44:05.324 --> 00:44:07.628
Oi. You mug.


00:44:08.940 --> 00:44:10.412
She belongs to Sikes.


00:44:10.443 --> 00:44:12.300
You think
I don't know that?


00:44:12.331 --> 00:44:13.485
I don't belong to anyone.


00:44:21.291 --> 00:44:22.317
We'll see.


00:44:50.251 --> 00:44:52.684
Oi, Batesy!
Batesy, look out!


00:45:03.723 --> 00:45:05.772
I love coming here.


00:45:05.803 --> 00:45:07.692
You almost forget
you're in the city.


00:45:08.204 --> 00:45:10.284
How do you know
about this place?


00:45:10.315 --> 00:45:13.196
Uh, Sikes brought me
here once.


00:45:14.891 --> 00:45:16.300
Why'd you bring me
here then?


00:45:17.291 --> 00:45:20.396
Because I wanted to.
Is that okay?


00:45:21.579 --> 00:45:22.860
Hmm?


00:45:29.388 --> 00:45:31.148
Red!


00:45:42.636 --> 00:45:44.587
Seriously, why did
you bring me here?


00:45:44.619 --> 00:45:46.476
Why wouldn't
I bring you here?


00:45:46.507 --> 00:45:48.747
I don't think your girlfriend
would be too happy if she knew.


00:45:48.779 --> 00:45:50.732
Mmm, never said
she was my girlfriend.


00:45:52.235 --> 00:45:53.516
Why didn't you tell me?


00:45:54.252 --> 00:45:55.532
Tell you what?


00:45:56.652 --> 00:45:58.060
That you're only into...


00:45:58.091 --> 00:46:00.972
Girls?
Never said that either.


00:46:03.723 --> 00:46:05.067
I'm so confused.


00:46:19.147 --> 00:46:20.908
Oi! What the hell
are you doing?


00:46:32.556 --> 00:46:34.828
Hey. Don't tell anyone
about this, yeah?


00:46:35.564 --> 00:46:38.284
Red, if this is about Sikes,
you don't need to be scared.


00:46:38.316 --> 00:46:40.460
It's not me
I'm scared for.


00:46:57.804 --> 00:46:59.884
Got you!


00:46:59.915 --> 00:47:02.476
You think you're clever, don't you?
Call the police, love.


00:47:02.507 --> 00:47:04.844
- I will 'cause you're assaulting him!
- Assaulting him?


00:47:04.875 --> 00:47:07.659
- Yeah!
- This little bellend has been vandalizing property


00:47:07.692 --> 00:47:11.052
of the council with his
shitty little paintings.


00:47:11.083 --> 00:47:12.812
You wanna go as well, eh?


00:47:12.843 --> 00:47:14.123
Come on!


00:47:14.154 --> 00:47:16.267
Here they are.
Get down there, you! Go on.


00:47:16.300 --> 00:47:19.148
She's with the bellend there.
Arrest them.


00:47:19.179 --> 00:47:21.003
- Stay with them. It'll be okay.
- Come on, Son.


00:47:21.452 --> 00:47:22.700
I'll get Fagin.
Go on.


00:47:22.732 --> 00:47:24.428
Thank you.
All right.


00:47:32.364 --> 00:47:34.060
Personally I think
it's an improvement.


00:47:35.851 --> 00:47:37.005
So let me go.


00:47:37.771 --> 00:47:40.747
Unfortunately,
Metropolis Parking Solutions...


00:47:40.778 --> 00:47:42.891
That's the company
whose property you vandalized,


00:47:42.924 --> 00:47:45.709
they don't quite share
the same views.


00:47:50.956 --> 00:47:52.588
Little Ollie Twister.


00:47:58.506 --> 00:48:01.036
Look, to be honest, Oliver,
a little bit of graffiti


00:48:01.068 --> 00:48:03.340
is not really
what concerns me.


00:48:03.755 --> 00:48:05.771
You kind of running
into Warden Bumble,


00:48:05.804 --> 00:48:07.596
well that's just kind
of fortuitous for me.


00:48:07.628 --> 00:48:09.004
It's like
a happy accident.


00:48:09.739 --> 00:48:11.980
What I really wanna talk
to you about is...


00:48:15.595 --> 00:48:17.164
this man.


00:48:18.539 --> 00:48:19.564
Fagin.


00:48:20.394 --> 00:48:22.347
An alias, obviously.


00:48:22.379 --> 00:48:24.907
A once prestigious
art dealer.


00:48:24.939 --> 00:48:26.668
Then out of the blue...


00:48:26.699 --> 00:48:28.332
...vanishes.
Disappears.


00:48:29.003 --> 00:48:31.691
And since then, it seems
like he's been putting


00:48:31.724 --> 00:48:34.413
his knowledge of art
to more practical usage.


00:48:34.924 --> 00:48:37.645
Apparently he's running
quite the operation.


00:48:39.916 --> 00:48:41.229
Yeah.


00:48:42.315 --> 00:48:43.979
And what about
this lovely lady?


00:48:44.011 --> 00:48:45.516
Known associate of Fagin.


00:48:45.546 --> 00:48:46.892
Sikes.


00:48:48.363 --> 00:48:50.092
How am I supposed
to know these two?


00:48:51.914 --> 00:48:53.547
How am I supposed to...


00:48:55.147 --> 00:48:57.612
Nancy Lee, alias Red.


00:48:57.643 --> 00:49:00.555
Known associate of
both Sikes and Fagin's.


00:49:03.851 --> 00:49:05.547
It's a pretty girl,
Oliver.


00:49:11.531 --> 00:49:13.131
I can get you out of this,
you know.


00:49:13.899 --> 00:49:16.651
- Get me out of what?
- Ah, see, now that,


00:49:16.682 --> 00:49:18.987
that's exactly what I'm
hoping you're gonna tell me.


00:49:19.020 --> 00:49:20.652
Because your little friends,
your new pals,


00:49:20.684 --> 00:49:23.373
they're not all
that they seem.


00:49:23.852 --> 00:49:26.252
And to be perfectly honest,
friends of Fagin and Sikes


00:49:26.283 --> 00:49:28.172
have a nasty habit
of ending up, well...


00:49:31.659 --> 00:49:33.228
like that.


00:49:33.258 --> 00:49:35.531
Tom Chitling.
He died last month.


00:49:35.564 --> 00:49:37.932
Take a good look, Oliver.


00:49:37.963 --> 00:49:39.212
I don't even know this Sikes.


00:49:40.267 --> 00:49:41.932
Are you sure?


00:49:43.084 --> 00:49:44.589
I'm sure.


00:49:46.603 --> 00:49:47.629
Okay.


00:49:48.235 --> 00:49:50.315
Well,
you're free to go.


00:49:51.338 --> 00:49:54.603
Just be careful who you trust because
people only see what they wanna see.


00:49:57.067 --> 00:49:58.251
Off you go, then.


00:50:07.211 --> 00:50:08.556
You're late.


00:50:09.899 --> 00:50:11.403
Where's Twist?


00:50:12.491 --> 00:50:13.740
He was with you,
right, Dodge?


00:50:18.796 --> 00:50:21.196
Just wanted to get a run-in.
I lost track of time.


00:50:22.154 --> 00:50:23.468
I don't know
where Twist is.


00:50:23.499 --> 00:50:25.419
I gave them all the night off.


00:50:25.450 --> 00:50:28.171
Those paintings are going
nowhere till the morning.


00:50:28.204 --> 00:50:29.899
It is morning.
Where is he?


00:50:43.564 --> 00:50:45.356
- Who is this?
- <i>Think of me</i>


00:50:45.387 --> 00:50:47.403
<i>as the friendly uncle
you never had.</i>


00:50:47.435 --> 00:50:49.739
<i>I just wanted to make sure
you've got my number.</i>


00:50:50.380 --> 00:50:52.940
<i>In case you remember anything
about our Ms. Sikes.</i>


00:50:52.972 --> 00:50:54.221
I won't.


00:50:54.956 --> 00:50:57.100
You got some explaining
to do, boy.


00:50:58.955 --> 00:51:01.739
- Where you been, then?
- I went to a pub with Dodge and Batesy.


00:51:01.770 --> 00:51:04.203
They got back hours ago.
What happened to you?


00:51:05.195 --> 00:51:08.363
- I got arrested.
- Been having little words, have we?


00:51:08.395 --> 00:51:09.644
No, it wasn't
like that.


00:51:09.676 --> 00:51:11.308
It was this traffic warden.


00:51:11.339 --> 00:51:12.972
I wrote on his van
and he wasn't happy about it.


00:51:13.002 --> 00:51:14.796
You wrote
on his van last night?


00:51:14.827 --> 00:51:16.363
No, last week.


00:51:16.396 --> 00:51:18.059
I bumped into him
this morning...


00:51:18.091 --> 00:51:19.692
How come
the cops let you go?


00:51:20.491 --> 00:51:22.411
Did you give them
something they wanted?


00:51:22.443 --> 00:51:24.300
No, nothing.
I gave them nothing.


00:51:24.332 --> 00:51:25.708
If he grassed,
why would he come back here?


00:51:25.739 --> 00:51:26.892
Was I talking to you?


00:51:26.924 --> 00:51:28.780
- I'm just saying, I...
- Don't!


00:51:28.811 --> 00:51:31.083
- We need him.
- <i>Hello, Artnet.</i>


00:51:31.115 --> 00:51:33.195
- <i>Hello, it's Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>
- Shh!


00:51:33.228 --> 00:51:35.243
<i>My vault is flooded, so I need
to move a painting to Dotheboy's.</i>


00:51:35.274 --> 00:51:36.971
He's on the phone
with the couriers.


00:51:37.002 --> 00:51:38.348
They're arranging a pickup.


00:51:38.379 --> 00:51:39.819
<i>One second.</i>


00:51:41.131 --> 00:51:42.795
Round three.


00:51:43.978 --> 00:51:45.707
The painting is gonna be
on the move.


00:51:45.738 --> 00:51:47.467
This is it.


00:51:47.498 --> 00:51:49.675
You better pray this time
it goes like clockwork.


00:51:52.332 --> 00:51:54.700
Remember,
I'm watching.


00:52:03.404 --> 00:52:05.548
I'm claustrophobic,
okay.


00:52:05.579 --> 00:52:08.012
Nobody told me that
it was gonna be that small.


00:52:08.427 --> 00:52:10.988
- Quit making a fuss and get in.
- I'm not making a fuss.


00:52:11.020 --> 00:52:13.738
I'm claustrophobic.
It's an actual condition.


00:52:13.771 --> 00:52:16.267
If Batesy gets in there
and passes out,


00:52:16.299 --> 00:52:18.156
the whole plan's screwed.
What are we gonna do?


00:52:18.187 --> 00:52:20.172
Exactly. And there is
every chance


00:52:20.203 --> 00:52:22.252
that if I get in there
I will pass out.


00:52:22.283 --> 00:52:24.076
Batesy,
don't be such a baby.


00:52:24.107 --> 00:52:26.123
What are you gonna do?
Force him down?


00:52:26.155 --> 00:52:28.235
You say you're gonna do
something then don't do it.


00:52:28.266 --> 00:52:31.564
Are we gonna do this,
or you gonna stand there arguing all day?


00:52:31.595 --> 00:52:32.684
Well, he's in now.


00:52:33.834 --> 00:52:36.972
All right. Anybody tries
to moves the crate,


00:52:37.004 --> 00:52:39.500
you set off the smoke bomb
in their face.


00:52:40.331 --> 00:52:41.515
Piece of cake.


00:52:42.186 --> 00:52:43.627
All right. That's it.


00:52:45.931 --> 00:52:46.923
Let's do it then.


00:52:50.218 --> 00:52:51.308
Really?


00:53:02.955 --> 00:53:05.163
Delivery to our gallery
in W1, yeah?


00:53:05.195 --> 00:53:06.475
Yeah, copy that, darling.


00:53:06.508 --> 00:53:07.948
We just got
a few drop-offs first.


00:53:07.980 --> 00:53:09.132
Cheers, lads.


00:53:33.035 --> 00:53:35.563
I thought we were only sharing travel
with the National Gallery piece.


00:53:35.595 --> 00:53:37.131
Uh, let me see.


00:53:37.162 --> 00:53:38.796
Originally yours
was dropped off first


00:53:38.827 --> 00:53:40.172
and then on
to the National Gallery.


00:53:40.203 --> 00:53:41.868
It's just an extra
pickup, mate.


00:53:41.898 --> 00:53:43.244
It won't affect
your drop-off time.


00:53:43.274 --> 00:53:45.642
They're close together,
you see.


00:53:45.674 --> 00:53:49.515
- Chiswell Fine Arts.
- I've never heard of it.


00:53:56.107 --> 00:53:58.507
You ever heard of
a Chiswell Fine Arts, Rosie?


00:53:58.539 --> 00:54:00.075
Somewhere near here?


00:54:00.490 --> 00:54:02.699
I thought you knew all
the galleries in London.


00:54:05.579 --> 00:54:07.563
I'll google it.


00:54:13.482 --> 00:54:15.884
Can't find a Chiswell.


00:54:18.603 --> 00:54:20.363
Get me Artnet
on the phone now!


00:54:41.611 --> 00:54:43.276
What's all this?


00:54:49.898 --> 00:54:51.179
You all right?
What's occurring?


00:54:51.210 --> 00:54:53.068
- Can we get through?
- How you doing?


00:54:53.098 --> 00:54:54.508
- Yeah, fine.
- Where you from?


00:54:54.539 --> 00:54:56.075
- I'm from Fullham.
- Fullham?


00:54:56.106 --> 00:54:58.891
I've got cousins in Fullham.
You know Phil?


00:54:58.923 --> 00:55:00.843
- No.
- You must know my second cousin.


00:55:00.875 --> 00:55:02.635
- What's her name? Oh, Tracey.
- No.


00:55:02.667 --> 00:55:04.459
- Can we get through?
- Can you get through?


00:55:04.491 --> 00:55:06.603
I don't know...


00:55:06.635 --> 00:55:09.196
<i>7-4, receiving. 7-4, receiving.</i>


00:55:09.226 --> 00:55:11.052
Is there aliens?
I mean...


00:55:11.082 --> 00:55:12.491
7-4. Go ahead.


00:55:12.523 --> 00:55:14.667
<i>Just had a call from
the Losberne Gallery.</i>


00:55:14.700 --> 00:55:16.939
<i>They seem to think
they're being robbed.</i>


00:55:16.971 --> 00:55:19.915
Is it real?
Is life even real?


00:55:19.947 --> 00:55:21.387
Everything all right,
lads?


00:55:22.475 --> 00:55:24.011
Floor it!


00:55:38.218 --> 00:55:39.819
No!


00:55:41.324 --> 00:55:43.467
Sikes, no.
No, Sikes!


00:55:44.011 --> 00:55:45.516
Please, Sikes.


00:55:48.491 --> 00:55:49.611
Run!


00:55:50.572 --> 00:55:53.419
- Where is it? Give it to me.
- I didn't get it. I'm sorry.


00:55:53.451 --> 00:55:56.491
We need a distraction.
Move. Move!


00:56:01.194 --> 00:56:03.242
When I said "don't,"
that means don't go this way.


00:56:03.275 --> 00:56:05.611
- <i>...female in a red leather jacket.</i>
- Hey!


00:56:05.642 --> 00:56:07.626
Female suspect heading west
down Pass Road.


00:56:07.659 --> 00:56:10.027
<i>Officers are in pursuit.
Officers are in pursuit.</i>


00:56:22.860 --> 00:56:24.428
I'm asking you
very nicely to stop.


00:56:28.075 --> 00:56:29.324
There it is.


00:56:53.738 --> 00:56:55.660
I really need
to start going to the gym.


00:56:56.555 --> 00:56:57.675
This is...


00:57:08.299 --> 00:57:09.548
Uh...


00:57:11.242 --> 00:57:12.970
<i>Bedwin, give me an update.</i>


00:57:13.002 --> 00:57:15.211
Brownlow, we got some good news
and some bad news.


00:57:15.243 --> 00:57:17.706
- <i>Fill me in then.</i>
- Yeah, well, the bad news is I haven't got her.


00:57:17.834 --> 00:57:20.875
- <i>What's the good news?</i>
- There is no good news, really, if I'm honest.


00:57:20.907 --> 00:57:22.603
<i>Get yourself back here now.</i>


00:57:29.547 --> 00:57:31.083
Oi! Get in.


00:57:31.884 --> 00:57:34.123
- I need to work on my cardio.
- How come Twist was


00:57:34.155 --> 00:57:35.884
in the back of that van?
Should have been you.


00:57:36.779 --> 00:57:40.043
Well, I'm claustrophobic,
so we just switched places.


00:57:42.540 --> 00:57:43.884
You shouldn't have.


00:57:50.827 --> 00:57:52.364
Batesy!


00:58:27.946 --> 00:58:29.674
He should have been
back by now.


00:58:29.706 --> 00:58:31.659
Quiet. I'm trying to think.


00:58:32.108 --> 00:58:34.315
That was our one shot.


00:58:35.754 --> 00:58:37.706
It was bad luck
is all.


00:58:38.155 --> 00:58:39.659
Bad luck? There's no such thing.


00:58:39.691 --> 00:58:42.347
It was a simple plan
until that bloody Twist


00:58:42.379 --> 00:58:44.554
decided to go in the van.


00:58:50.794 --> 00:58:52.652
Mate, have you seen...


00:58:54.923 --> 00:58:56.491
What happened
to Tom Chitling?


00:58:56.523 --> 00:58:57.611
He fell.


00:58:59.370 --> 00:59:03.210
- Did you see it?
- Someone has been misinforming you, Oliver.


00:59:03.243 --> 00:59:07.659
- Don't avoid the question!
- I just don't think it's you asking the questions.


00:59:07.691 --> 00:59:09.612
Who have you been talking to?


00:59:12.267 --> 00:59:13.772
Sikes.


00:59:14.378 --> 00:59:16.587
Why don't you ask her?


00:59:17.707 --> 00:59:19.499
- Sikes!
- He's a rat!


00:59:19.979 --> 00:59:22.027
Van suddenly peels off.
They knew what was going down.


00:59:22.059 --> 00:59:23.468
- I didn't tell them anything!
- Lies!


00:59:25.515 --> 00:59:26.859
What's this, eh?


00:59:29.483 --> 00:59:31.307
Thing I need to know, Twist,


00:59:31.339 --> 00:59:33.067
is how you hold up
under a beating.


00:59:33.611 --> 00:59:34.954
I bet you fall
to pieces, eh?


00:59:34.987 --> 00:59:36.203
Fagin, make her stop.


00:59:44.746 --> 00:59:46.474
Question is,
do you want some more?


00:59:49.259 --> 00:59:50.380
Hold him.


00:59:51.723 --> 00:59:53.802
Sikes, don't make it
permanent.


00:59:53.834 --> 00:59:55.563
Right, Bullseye,
on my command.


00:59:57.002 --> 00:59:58.954
You're making a mistake.


00:59:59.434 --> 01:00:00.843
A mistake?


01:00:01.706 --> 01:00:03.628
He got in trouble
with the traffic warden.


01:00:03.659 --> 01:00:05.516
And how would
you know that, Red?


01:00:06.154 --> 01:00:07.532
'Cause I was there.


01:00:08.650 --> 01:00:09.771
What?


01:00:12.011 --> 01:00:13.867
We were on our way home
and the traffic warden


01:00:13.899 --> 01:00:15.723
came out of nowhere
and tackled him to the ground.


01:00:15.755 --> 01:00:17.707
- Just like he said.
- On your way home from where?


01:00:20.298 --> 01:00:21.387
We...


01:00:22.603 --> 01:00:24.460
We went for a swim together.


01:00:37.451 --> 01:00:39.275
If he moves, shoot him.


01:00:39.307 --> 01:00:41.355
Come with me.


01:00:41.386 --> 01:00:42.603
Bullseye, stay.


01:00:55.275 --> 01:00:56.971
This ain't like Batesy.


01:00:57.002 --> 01:00:58.986
He gets withdrawal symptoms
if he ain't plugged in.


01:00:59.019 --> 01:01:01.323
- Batesy's dead.
- What?


01:01:01.354 --> 01:01:02.635
Just like she killed Tom.


01:01:03.210 --> 01:01:05.290
- But Sikes said...
- Tom was murdered!


01:01:06.026 --> 01:01:08.170
He didn't go off
that roof by accident.


01:01:09.451 --> 01:01:10.859
How would you know that?


01:01:12.011 --> 01:01:13.260
I got a text
off that phone.


01:01:14.826 --> 01:01:16.362
Some cop gave it to me
to see if I'd turn.


01:01:16.395 --> 01:01:18.123
And did you turn?


01:01:18.155 --> 01:01:21.100
Or were you never
with this family to begin with?


01:01:21.610 --> 01:01:23.275
You call this a family?


01:01:23.979 --> 01:01:25.546
When that psycho is
out there with Red


01:01:25.579 --> 01:01:27.179
and you're pointing
a gun at me!


01:01:28.331 --> 01:01:29.547
I don't believe you.


01:01:29.578 --> 01:01:31.114
I'm gonna go find Batesy myself.


01:01:31.147 --> 01:01:32.652
You're gonna be looking
six feet under.


01:01:33.099 --> 01:01:35.883
He's right. I pushed Tom.


01:01:35.914 --> 01:01:37.770
- You lying piece...
- Please.


01:01:37.802 --> 01:01:39.595
Give me an excuse to kill you.


01:01:40.011 --> 01:01:41.227
You can't kill all of us.


01:01:41.994 --> 01:01:43.179
Let's see, shall we?


01:01:43.755 --> 01:01:45.963
Six bullets, three kids.
You do the math.


01:01:45.995 --> 01:01:48.331
We're hitting Dotheboy's.
We're getting that painting.


01:01:48.363 --> 01:01:50.219
Dotheboy's?
I think the whole plan


01:01:50.250 --> 01:01:52.746
was to get the painting
before it went there.


01:01:52.778 --> 01:01:54.987
That place
is impenetrable.


01:01:55.019 --> 01:01:56.619
You scared, old man?


01:01:57.130 --> 01:01:59.531
I'll have a plan
in four hours.


01:02:00.042 --> 01:02:03.083
Try not to kill any more
of them in the meantime.


01:02:05.738 --> 01:02:07.051
I can't promise anything.


01:02:15.498 --> 01:02:17.610
<i>Look, mate,
I believe ya.</i>


01:02:18.283 --> 01:02:20.619
<i>What Sikes did to Tom,
that's messed up.</i>


01:02:21.194 --> 01:02:23.499
But if we don't do this,
we'll lose Red too.


01:02:25.003 --> 01:02:26.763
Sikes is a loose cannon.


01:02:26.794 --> 01:02:28.843
Let's just suck it up
and get on with it, yeah?


01:02:30.538 --> 01:02:31.883
Let's do this.


01:02:38.570 --> 01:02:39.658
<i>Is he on time?</i>


01:02:39.690 --> 01:02:42.380
Like clockwork. We're on.


01:02:54.827 --> 01:02:56.491
Can I get two sugars
with that, as well?


01:02:57.226 --> 01:02:58.954
All right there, mates?
Sorry to interrupt.


01:02:58.986 --> 01:03:00.810
Can I get a Bakewell tart,
please?


01:03:00.842 --> 01:03:02.347
Sure.


01:03:02.859 --> 01:03:04.683
- It's chippy, innit?
- Yeah, I know. It's freezing.


01:03:04.715 --> 01:03:06.443
There you go. 1.50.


01:03:06.892 --> 01:03:08.234
There you go.
Keep the change.


01:03:09.482 --> 01:03:10.572
Thanks.


01:03:12.811 --> 01:03:14.122
Have a good day,
lads.


01:03:14.154 --> 01:03:15.339
See ya.


01:03:29.674 --> 01:03:33.130
<i>The painting will be under
lock and key before the auction.</i>


01:03:33.546 --> 01:03:36.491
<i>So our only chance is
during the main event.</i>


01:03:36.522 --> 01:03:39.210
<i>We'll go in at the front
and at the right moment</i>


01:03:39.243 --> 01:03:42.123
<i>execute the plan,
sending the painting your way.</i>


01:03:42.154 --> 01:03:44.171
Let's play happy families, eh?
Big smiles.


01:04:02.059 --> 01:04:03.723
Thank you.


01:04:03.754 --> 01:04:05.674
Whoa, whoa.


01:04:05.706 --> 01:04:07.723
It's the chair. Really?


01:04:08.235 --> 01:04:09.419
Jesus.


01:04:26.026 --> 01:04:28.042
There you go.


01:04:28.074 --> 01:04:30.699
<i>Dodge, once you're
inside, let Twist in.</i>


01:04:30.731 --> 01:04:32.810
<i>Then, when all hell
has broken loose,</i>


01:04:32.842 --> 01:04:33.962
<i>you know what to do.</i>


01:04:39.403 --> 01:04:40.651
Gang's all here.


01:04:49.130 --> 01:04:50.923
Don't do anything stupid.


01:04:59.883 --> 01:05:02.730
I'm glad you're finally taking
this threat seriously, Officer.


01:05:04.394 --> 01:05:05.996
Detective Inspector.


01:05:12.362 --> 01:05:13.772
How many men
have you deployed?


01:05:14.891 --> 01:05:16.235
There's 12
inside the building.


01:05:17.066 --> 01:05:18.763
Another 20 outside.


01:05:22.410 --> 01:05:23.915
Nobody is getting
this painting, Losberne.


01:05:23.946 --> 01:05:25.579
Doctor Losberne.


01:05:35.562 --> 01:05:37.194
Better you than me,
mate.


01:05:53.418 --> 01:05:54.987
<i>Lot 146.</i>


01:05:55.723 --> 01:05:57.514
William Hogarth's painting


01:05:57.546 --> 01:06:00.235
<i>A Harlot's Progress,
The Arrest.</i>


01:06:00.266 --> 01:06:03.146
Oil on canvas. 1731.


01:06:03.178 --> 01:06:05.258
Has resurfaced
after many years,


01:06:05.290 --> 01:06:08.042
as the only surviving <i>Harlot's
Progress</i> from the fire...


01:06:08.074 --> 01:06:09.579
Now.


01:06:10.155 --> 01:06:13.739
We start the reserve
price of three million pounds.


01:06:13.769 --> 01:06:15.242
Yes, madam.


01:06:16.618 --> 01:06:19.370
And you, sir? At the back there, sir? Yes.


01:06:19.403 --> 01:06:21.003
Three million two.


01:06:21.035 --> 01:06:22.571
I have three million,
200 thousand pounds.


01:06:24.841 --> 01:06:26.347
He's got a gun!


01:06:28.299 --> 01:06:30.219
- Stay calm.
- It was a trap.


01:06:30.249 --> 01:06:32.938
- They're after my painting!
- Get it back in the vault!


01:06:32.970 --> 01:06:34.635
It'll be safe.
It's the safest place.


01:06:39.915 --> 01:06:42.314
- Over there, look.
- Through that door.


01:06:47.082 --> 01:06:49.803
There's a robbery in progress.
Stay with the painting.


01:06:49.835 --> 01:06:51.691
Get it to the vault.
Let's go! Let's move.


01:06:54.922 --> 01:06:56.842
Wait, wait, wait.


01:06:56.874 --> 01:06:58.539
I'm coming with you.


01:06:58.570 --> 01:06:59.883
No one goes
down there but us.


01:06:59.914 --> 01:07:01.675
There's a robbery in progress.


01:07:01.707 --> 01:07:04.586
- Yeah, we have our procedures.
- And I have my orders.


01:07:04.619 --> 01:07:07.371
And that painting ain't going
anywhere without me.


01:07:07.403 --> 01:07:09.355
What... What's going on?


01:07:09.386 --> 01:07:12.171
- Who are you?
- Officer Dawkins, Sergeant.


01:07:12.202 --> 01:07:13.962
- Dawkins? Good.
- Yeah.


01:07:55.723 --> 01:07:58.507
Okay. You guys go that way.
You guys come with me. Let's go.


01:08:04.746 --> 01:08:05.930
You.


01:08:06.602 --> 01:08:08.971
Yes, it's me.


01:08:10.601 --> 01:08:12.554
Ah, that felt good.


01:08:28.170 --> 01:08:30.219
Good. This is good.
This is very good.


01:08:31.242 --> 01:08:32.748
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


01:08:36.010 --> 01:08:37.196
Show me the painting.


01:08:38.793 --> 01:08:39.786
Ah...


01:08:41.642 --> 01:08:43.498
I'll be honest,
not his best work.


01:08:47.338 --> 01:08:48.747
Move!


01:08:48.778 --> 01:08:49.771
Okay.


01:08:53.866 --> 01:08:55.690
Oh, you silly sausage.


01:08:55.722 --> 01:08:57.003
You're going nowhere, Son.


01:08:58.857 --> 01:09:00.363
Shit!


01:09:02.315 --> 01:09:04.330
Brownlow,
you're wrong about Twist.


01:09:04.362 --> 01:09:05.803
He's in the lift shaft.


01:09:05.834 --> 01:09:07.562
Yeah, the dirty swine.


01:09:09.066 --> 01:09:10.540
Well, move then.


01:09:14.218 --> 01:09:16.234
I'm coming for you, Twist.


01:09:16.265 --> 01:09:19.179
- No, no, no!
- If you think a lift is gonna stop me...


01:09:20.075 --> 01:09:22.891
- Oh, you got nowhere to hide, boy.
- Dodge!


01:09:22.923 --> 01:09:23.979
- You muppet.
- Dodge?


01:09:24.010 --> 01:09:25.834
You...


01:09:25.865 --> 01:09:26.922
Hurry up.


01:09:26.954 --> 01:09:28.138
- Dodge.
- Come on.


01:09:28.170 --> 01:09:29.418
Help me!


01:09:29.451 --> 01:09:31.339
- Hurry up.
- Help!


01:09:31.370 --> 01:09:33.355
- Come on.
- I'm coming!


01:09:33.387 --> 01:09:35.019
Get these bloody doors open!


01:09:44.458 --> 01:09:45.707
Hurry up, Dodge!


01:09:59.241 --> 01:10:00.746
Oi!


01:10:07.145 --> 01:10:08.681
Wait a minute.


01:10:08.713 --> 01:10:10.666
Give me a break.
You're not thinking we...


01:10:10.698 --> 01:10:12.875
- Oi! Stop!
- Come on!


01:10:15.498 --> 01:10:18.059
- Ready? Belt.
- Twist, what are you doing? This is madness.


01:10:18.089 --> 01:10:19.658
Three, two, one...


01:10:22.954 --> 01:10:24.138
Hang on!


01:10:24.938 --> 01:10:26.443
Wait, wait...


01:10:26.474 --> 01:10:27.658
Let go!


01:10:33.610 --> 01:10:35.402
Okay.


01:10:35.434 --> 01:10:36.682
Congratulations.


01:10:37.707 --> 01:10:38.827
All the best.


01:10:42.538 --> 01:10:44.427
Brownlow, you need
to get down here right now.


01:10:49.865 --> 01:10:51.114
Shit!


01:10:51.146 --> 01:10:54.506
Shit, shit!


01:10:54.538 --> 01:10:56.618
- Flippin' hell.
- Let's go up here.


01:10:58.537 --> 01:11:00.299
I think we've lost them.


01:11:00.329 --> 01:11:02.379
They wouldn't have got far,
Losberne.


01:11:02.410 --> 01:11:03.754
Well,
you better be right.


01:11:04.394 --> 01:11:06.186
- Come on. Let's go.
- Hey! Hey!


01:11:06.217 --> 01:11:07.723
Don't even think about it!
Do not move.


01:11:07.753 --> 01:11:10.025
Hello?


01:11:10.057 --> 01:11:12.106
- <i>Your delivery's here.</i>
- I didn't order anything.


01:11:12.843 --> 01:11:15.243
- Hey, don't!
- Dodge, let's go!


01:11:16.234 --> 01:11:17.706
Hey!


01:11:17.738 --> 01:11:19.755
Get after them!
Don't leave, hey!


01:11:19.785 --> 01:11:21.835
- Come back here! Come...
- Wait!


01:11:21.866 --> 01:11:24.874
Get them... Hey, stop!


01:11:24.905 --> 01:11:27.466
Stop! Make him stop!


01:11:44.907 --> 01:11:47.691
There's only one person
who could do this.


01:11:53.770 --> 01:11:55.306
<i>Batesy.</i>


01:11:55.337 --> 01:11:56.650
Enjoy your munch, did ya?


01:11:56.682 --> 01:11:59.178
You magnificent bastard.


01:11:59.211 --> 01:12:03.082
You had us worried sick, mate.
Where are ya?


01:12:03.113 --> 01:12:05.930
You know Sikes has gone
full-blown psycho, don't you?


01:12:05.962 --> 01:12:07.625
- <i>She tried to kill me.</i>
- What?


01:12:07.658 --> 01:12:09.131
We're on our way
to see her now.


01:12:09.162 --> 01:12:10.986
<i>No, don't! It ain't safe.</i>


01:12:11.018 --> 01:12:13.515
What do you mean?
We got no choice.


01:12:13.546 --> 01:12:15.691
<i>Red's with her.
We're all heading to Fagin's.</i>


01:12:16.843 --> 01:12:18.475
All right, well,
I'll meet you there.


01:12:18.507 --> 01:12:20.011
- <i>Just look after yourself.</i>
- Okay.


01:12:21.193 --> 01:12:23.242
That was Batesy. He's...


01:12:25.834 --> 01:12:27.018
Twist?


01:12:31.498 --> 01:12:32.714
Twist?


01:12:36.457 --> 01:12:38.283
You're late.
Where is he?


01:12:38.857 --> 01:12:40.586
I don't know.
We got split up.


01:12:40.617 --> 01:12:42.185
- Who's got it?
- He has.


01:12:42.218 --> 01:12:43.435
Oi!


01:12:44.362 --> 01:12:46.506
- You miss me?
- Bates.


01:12:47.082 --> 01:12:48.906
You all right?
What happened?


01:12:48.937 --> 01:12:51.051
Thought I dealt with you,
fuck's sake.


01:12:51.081 --> 01:12:53.161
- Where's Twist?
- I'm right here.


01:13:01.002 --> 01:13:02.858
You want the painting?
She's coming with me.


01:13:04.139 --> 01:13:05.579
Do you think she's worth it?


01:13:09.321 --> 01:13:10.314
Try me.


01:13:11.850 --> 01:13:13.451
Do what he says.


01:13:18.058 --> 01:13:20.139
You got more stones than
I gave you credit for.


01:13:21.929 --> 01:13:23.435
Give me that.


01:13:29.289 --> 01:13:31.242
I'll always be
a step ahead of you.


01:13:34.633 --> 01:13:36.490
You think
you can just take my girl?


01:13:37.865 --> 01:13:38.890
It's the painting, Sikes.


01:13:39.337 --> 01:13:41.546
Give me the envelope
and let him go.


01:13:42.634 --> 01:13:43.754
You sure that's it, Fagin?


01:13:48.650 --> 01:13:50.571
- What?
- The painting.


01:13:51.241 --> 01:13:52.618
Are you sure
it's the right one?


01:13:57.322 --> 01:13:59.211
Easy. Easy.


01:13:59.785 --> 01:14:01.450
I'm just reaching for my phone.


01:14:02.025 --> 01:14:03.946
You guys might wanna see this.


01:14:09.898 --> 01:14:11.755
You see,
before I got into graffiti,


01:14:12.522 --> 01:14:14.187
I used to paint.


01:14:14.218 --> 01:14:17.481
You lot mentioning Hogarth
got me inspired.


01:14:17.514 --> 01:14:19.339
It's not bad, eh, Fagin?


01:14:20.105 --> 01:14:21.290
Where is it?


01:14:21.673 --> 01:14:23.371
I walk out of here
with Red.


01:14:24.105 --> 01:14:25.898
I'll call you
and tell you where it is.


01:14:25.929 --> 01:14:27.275
She stays with me.


01:14:28.681 --> 01:14:30.282
We need the painting, Sikes.


01:14:30.313 --> 01:14:32.170
Whose side are you on?


01:14:32.202 --> 01:14:35.307
All this has got to stop.
You're done. We're done.


01:14:35.339 --> 01:14:37.323
All bets are off.


01:14:37.354 --> 01:14:40.426
Get me the envelope
and I'll let you leave.


01:14:53.898 --> 01:14:55.081
Come on.


01:14:55.978 --> 01:14:57.513
You'll let me leave?


01:15:03.754 --> 01:15:05.450
I choose how this ends.


01:15:06.473 --> 01:15:08.107
- Fagin, Fagin.
- Fagin.


01:15:08.618 --> 01:15:09.611
Fagin?


01:15:15.690 --> 01:15:17.066
Come on!


01:15:17.802 --> 01:15:19.946
Quick! Come on, Twist!


01:15:32.457 --> 01:15:33.866
Come on!


01:15:38.378 --> 01:15:39.819
You go first.


01:15:39.850 --> 01:15:41.291
I'm not going without you!


01:15:41.322 --> 01:15:43.563
Listen, jump.
I'll be right behind you.


01:15:44.073 --> 01:15:45.066
Go.


01:16:02.153 --> 01:16:03.945
Twist! Twist.


01:16:03.977 --> 01:16:05.226
Hold on, hold on.


01:16:05.257 --> 01:16:06.827
Come on!


01:16:11.594 --> 01:16:13.898
Twist! Come on.


01:16:13.930 --> 01:16:15.274
Don't let go.


01:16:22.889 --> 01:16:24.874
No! No!


01:16:27.819 --> 01:16:30.955
- Pull him up, Sikes.
- I'm sure he'll be fine. Step back!


01:16:30.985 --> 01:16:33.065
Look at him, not even strong
enough to pull himself up.


01:16:33.098 --> 01:16:35.626
- He's so weak.
- He's not weak!


01:16:35.658 --> 01:16:38.442
- You need to come with me now.
- I don't need you anymore.


01:16:38.473 --> 01:16:40.202
You think Twist is
the one for you?


01:16:40.233 --> 01:16:41.611
He's more than
you will ever be.


01:16:41.641 --> 01:16:43.339
I dragged you from the gutter,
looked after you,


01:16:43.370 --> 01:16:45.130
gave you everything
you needed.


01:16:45.161 --> 01:16:46.410
Sikes!


01:17:03.210 --> 01:17:06.443
What a fine thing
capital punishment is.


01:17:39.178 --> 01:17:40.651
Young man.


01:17:43.881 --> 01:17:45.802
I'm guessing you heard
about the reward?


01:17:49.865 --> 01:17:51.467
Be there in five.


01:17:56.489 --> 01:17:58.889
Do we know what we're meant
to be waiting for?


01:17:58.921 --> 01:18:01.099
We don't have a clue,
Bedwin.


01:18:01.129 --> 01:18:03.115
I'm sure we'll know
when we see it.


01:18:03.146 --> 01:18:05.291
He's not exactly just gonna stroll in.


01:18:05.321 --> 01:18:07.850
- He's literally just strolled in.
- All right, lads?


01:18:08.361 --> 01:18:10.761
- You hungry?
- You got a lot of nerve showing up.


01:18:10.793 --> 01:18:12.906
- Let's just nick him now.
- Calm down, Bedwin.


01:18:12.938 --> 01:18:14.602
You look like you could do
with a bacon sarnie.


01:18:14.634 --> 01:18:16.362
This might be funny to you,
but this is serious.


01:18:16.392 --> 01:18:17.609
I need your full cooperation.


01:18:17.642 --> 01:18:19.659
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Cooperation?


01:18:20.266 --> 01:18:21.835
I've done you guys a favor.


01:18:22.601 --> 01:18:24.234
How's that?


01:18:24.266 --> 01:18:25.354
Where's the painting?


01:18:25.384 --> 01:18:26.667
I don't have it.


01:18:26.698 --> 01:18:28.202
So where is it?


01:18:28.234 --> 01:18:29.961
I'm not the criminal here.
In fact,


01:18:29.994 --> 01:18:31.498
I've done all the work
for you guys.


01:18:31.529 --> 01:18:33.386
Two bacon sarnies.


01:18:33.417 --> 01:18:34.666
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


01:18:34.697 --> 01:18:36.330
Excuse me. I didn't order this.


01:18:36.362 --> 01:18:38.635
Oh, no, it's fine.
It's my treat.


01:18:38.665 --> 01:18:40.777
Well, that's very kind of you,
young man.


01:18:40.810 --> 01:18:43.978
- Yes, very kind.
- But don't think this is getting you out of trouble.


01:18:44.009 --> 01:18:45.322
I need you to understand
one thing.


01:18:45.353 --> 01:18:47.113
You're gonna need
to start cooperating.


01:18:50.409 --> 01:18:51.817
Oh, brilliant.


01:19:01.930 --> 01:19:03.882
Yeah, hello?
Very smart that was.


01:19:03.913 --> 01:19:05.577
<i>A wise cop
once said to me,</i>


01:19:05.608 --> 01:19:07.529
<i>"People only see
what they wanna see."</i>


01:19:07.561 --> 01:19:10.377
<i>You'll be wanting some
brown sauce with those I assume.</i>


01:19:10.408 --> 01:19:13.066
What do you mean... Hello? Hello?


01:19:15.817 --> 01:19:17.129
Brown sauce.


01:19:20.233 --> 01:19:21.513
Nah, it's...


01:19:25.033 --> 01:19:26.569
It's above
the brown sauce, Bedwin.


01:19:26.601 --> 01:19:28.107
It's above
the brown sauce.


01:19:30.153 --> 01:19:31.690
Holy shit.


01:19:45.897 --> 01:19:49.418
<i>The tale of the stolen Hogarth
in an audacious raid</i>


01:19:49.450 --> 01:19:51.402
<i>took a bizarre twist today</i>


01:19:51.432 --> 01:19:54.730
<i>when a tip-off led detectives
to a lockup in East London</i>


01:19:54.762 --> 01:19:58.570
<i>in which a large collection of
stolen artworks has been discovered.</i>


01:19:58.602 --> 01:20:02.731
<i>The lockup belongs to the art
dealer Dr. Crispin Losberne.</i>


01:20:03.305 --> 01:20:06.986
<i>Documents were also found
proving that Dr. Crispin Losberne</i>


01:20:07.017 --> 01:20:09.930
<i>is not the legal owner
of the Hogarth.</i>


01:20:09.962 --> 01:20:12.906
<i>It's alleged that
the well-established art dealer</i>


01:20:12.938 --> 01:20:16.459
<i>has been making his fortune
out of selling stolen artwork</i>


01:20:16.490 --> 01:20:19.082
<i>and faking
the ownership documentation.</i>


01:20:19.114 --> 01:20:22.506
<i>A Mr. Isaac Solomon
has been named as an accomplice.</i>


01:20:22.537 --> 01:20:26.059
<i>It's believed that this man
also goes by the name of Fagin.</i>


01:20:26.665 --> 01:20:29.258
<i>Fagin and Sikes really
had raised some good thieves.</i>


01:20:29.289 --> 01:20:32.105
<i>So good they didn't know
when they were the target.</i>


01:20:36.938 --> 01:20:39.466
<i>The envelope revealed
the true owners of the Hogarth</i>


01:20:39.497 --> 01:20:42.698
<i>and the key to the lockup where
Losberne kept the stolen paintings.</i>


01:20:53.033 --> 01:20:56.682
- Holy shit.
- <i>Even Bedwin and Brownlow deserved a break.</i>


01:20:56.712 --> 01:20:58.826
<i>In other arts-related news,</i>


01:20:58.857 --> 01:21:02.345
<i>a mystery painting arrived
with a special delivery</i>


01:21:02.376 --> 01:21:05.513
<i>for a new exhibition at
the National Gallery last week.</i>


01:21:05.545 --> 01:21:09.226
<i>The question everyone's asking
is: How did it get there?</i>


01:21:09.866 --> 01:21:12.969
<i>The painting was added
to the exhibition by mistake</i>


01:21:13.002 --> 01:21:16.138
<i>but critics have gone wild
for this unknown artist</i>


01:21:16.169 --> 01:21:18.890
<i>and have demanded
the piece remains on display.</i>


01:21:24.074 --> 01:21:25.514
There you go, Mum.


01:21:29.417 --> 01:21:33.353
<i>In fact, people can't stop
talking about the mystery artist,</i>


01:21:33.386 --> 01:21:36.106
<i>with many asking
who is Molly Twist</i>


01:21:36.137 --> 01:21:39.178
<i>and when and where
will all of her work appear.</i>


01:21:39.208 --> 01:21:42.569
<i>Dealers are said to be willing
to offer up to 50,000</i>


01:21:42.600 --> 01:21:45.609
<i>to anyone with
an original Twist painting.</i>


01:22:03.112 --> 01:22:04.713
Cheers, Nancy.


01:22:06.729 --> 01:22:09.577
Call me that again, Oliver,
and I will twist something you don't like.


01:22:11.849 --> 01:22:13.898
All right, quit canoodling.


01:22:16.552 --> 01:22:19.658
So, are you gonna stick
with us, kid?


01:22:19.689 --> 01:22:21.482
Come on,
you know you wanna.


01:22:21.514 --> 01:22:23.914
Look, if I'm gonna be
staying around,


01:22:23.945 --> 01:22:25.961
we gotta cut out all
the nonsense and go straight.


01:22:25.992 --> 01:22:29.161
- Whoa, wait.
- He's joking, right? That must be a joke.


01:22:29.193 --> 01:22:32.650
What exactly do you expect
us lot to do for a job, eh?


01:22:33.353 --> 01:22:35.306
You ever thought about
selling paintings?


01:22:36.266 --> 01:22:38.666
A bag full of Molly Twist art
is worth a few quid.


01:22:40.201 --> 01:22:41.194
Hmm?


01:22:41.993 --> 01:22:45.289
<i>Like I said, no singing,
no dancing.</i>


01:22:45.322 --> 01:22:47.402
<i>But maybe I was wrong about
the happy ending.</i>


01:22:48.362 --> 01:22:51.114
<i>I know these people.
I belong with them.</i>


01:25:39.082 --> 01:25:41.707
